{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1469059-inspiration-for-changeling-christmas-story","id":1469059,"title":"Inspiration for Changeling Christmas Story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-27T19:20:09-08:00","id":1469059,"title":"Inspiration for Changeling Christmas Story","content":"With Christmas just around the corner, I want to offer some sources of inspiration for a Changeling Christmas chronicle.<br /> <br /> The first is Brom's <b><i>Krampus: The Yule Lord.</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Santa Claus, my dear old friend, you are a thief, a traitor, a slanderer, a murder, a liar, but worst of all you are a mockery of everything for which I stood.</i><br /> <i>You have sung your last ho, ho, ho, for I am coming to take your head. I am coming to take back what is mine, to take back Yuletide...</i><br /> <br /> The author and artist of <i>The Child Thief</i> returns with a modern fabulist tale of Krampus, the Lord of Yule and mortal enemy of Santa Claus.<br /> <br /> One Christmas Eve in a small hollow in Boone County, West Virginia, struggling songwriter Jesse Walker witnesses a strange spectacle: seven devilish figures chasing a man in a red suit toward a sleigh and eight reindeer. When the reindeer leap skyward taking the sleigh, devil men, and Santa into the clouds, screams follow. Moments later, a large sack plummets earthward, a magical sack that will thrust the down-on-his luck singer into the clutches of the terrifying Yule Lord, Krampus. But the lines between good and evil become blurred as Jesse's new master reveals many dark secrets about the cherry-cheeked Santa Claus, and how half a millennium ago, the jolly old saint imprisoned Krampus and usurped his magic.<br /> <br /> Now Santa's time is running short, for the Yule Lord is determined to have his retribution and reclaim Yuletide. If Jesse can survive this ancient feud, he might have the chance to redeem himself to his family, to save his own broken dreams...and help bring the magic of Yule to the impoverished folk of Boone County.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Krampus</b></i> by Brom celebrates the mythology and folklore surrounding the pagan figure of Krampus, the Yule Lord, in a novel that is part fantasy, part horror, and part holiday treat. Though the legend of Krampus cuts across different cultures and takes many forms as a result, Brom selects a decidedly Norse leaning interpretation of the horned creature. Those familiar with Norse mythology will encounter many familiar personas (some directly and others by reference): there\u2019s Odin, Loki, Hel, Geri, Freki, Huginn, Muninn, and others.<br /> What I especially like about this story, is that it has a very strong <b><i>Changeling: The Lost</i></b> tone to it. Krampus\u2019 servant\u2019s the Belsnickels, are very similar to changelings. Family is also a strong theme in the story, though the character of Jesse.<br /> <br /> You can purchase the Kindle version on Amazon here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Krampus-Yule-Lord-Brom/dp/006209565X/ref=pd_sbs_4/144-2303566-9471821?pd_rd_w=hmA0i&amp;pf_rd_p=690958f6-2825-419e-9c16-73ffd4055b65&amp;pf_rd_r=241M8XXT5CQE5J8SXF30&amp;pd_rd_r=7eb25b43-e012-475d-9a3d-5cb07f282a60&amp;pd_rd_wg=MwXiy&amp;pd_rd_i=006209565X&amp;psc=1\" target=\"_blank\">Krampus: The Yule Lord: Brom: 9780062095657: Amazon.com: Books</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T19:24:20-08:00","id":1469060,"title":"","content":"Here is a lore book about another Christmas Monster Frau Perchta.<br /> <b>About Frau Perchta: Full Of Information About Various Forms Of The Perchta Legend: Christmas Season</b><br /><br /><span style=\"color:#0F1111\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the last few years Santa Claus\u2019 darker half, Krampus, has enjoyed a resurgence in popularity. The delightful half goat, half demon punishes where Santa Claus rewards. But he\u2019s not the only other Christmas-time folklore figure that kids can look forward to a visit from this holiday season. Christmas has often been the time for ghouls, ghosts, and stories by the crackling fire. Father Christmas has even had his evil twins like Krampus dealing out punishment for the children who misbehave all year round. However, there is a Christmas legend of a different kind that deals out punishment during the festive period; Frau Perchta, the Christmas belly-slitter. This book looks at the legend of the festive specter who is famous for her punishments but could also reward the well-behaved. Festivals in her honor continue to this day in the Alpine regions throughout Christmas. Enjoy this concise history of the legend of a Christmas creature in front of a warm festive fire.<br /> <br /> You can purchase the book here:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/About-Frau-Perchta-Information-Christmas/dp/B09917WX6T/ref=sr_1_1?keywords=Frau+Perchta&amp;qid=1638069695&amp;s=books&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">About Frau Perchta: Full Of Information About Various Forms Of The Perchta Legend: Christmas Season: Parral, Prudence: 9798534812794: Amazon.com: Books</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T19:34:56-08:00","id":1469062,"title":"","content":"<b>13 Days before Christmas: A Modern Tale of the Gryla</b><br /><br /><span style=\"color:#0F1111\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Over the years Christmas has developed its fair share of terrifying characters. Only recently the world was introduced to the famous Krampus. Now the historical Icelandic legend of the Gryla has emerged. This hideous troll-like creature and her thirteen sons have terrified the people of Iceland for generations. The literature you are holding is an account discovered recently from Reyjkavic-born, Stefan Ganurrson. If Christmas is truly a time of giving then Stefan truly offers everything in this powerful rhetoric of Christmas and Iceland's very own anti-Santa. Welcome to the cold, dark world of the Gryla and remember... if you hear a noise outside late on Christmas Eve, it is not always the jolly old man in red delivering gifts...<br /> <br /> <i>Note: This work is only 36 pages and pretty cheap. the Kindle version is $1.42 while the print version is $4.70<br /> <br /> You can purchase it here.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/13-Days-before-Christmas-Modern/dp/B08R4KBMZT/ref=sr_1_1?keywords=Gryla&amp;qid=1638070194&amp;s=books&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">13 Days before Christmas: A Modern Tale of the Gryla: Rome, W A: 9798579255181: Amazon.com: Books</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T21:51:58-08:00","id":1469069,"title":"","content":"I was lucky enough to find a story on youtube called <b><i>Krampus Night.</i></b> It has a very strong Changeling: The Lost tone to it, which will become apparent once you listen to it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3reJG-yunCk&amp;t=24s\" target=\"_blank\">Krampus Night - (Dark World Ep.1) - YouTube</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T22:57:57-08:00","id":1469071,"title":"","content":"P.S. I forgot to mention that I have seen the Brom's, <i><b>Krampus: </b></i><b><i>The Yule Lord </i></b>at both Barnes and Noble where I live. If possible, I recommend you buy it in book format at your local book store.<br /> <br /> ....Yes, this is me encouraging people to support book stores<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T13:55:43-08:00","id":1469122,"title":"","content":"Here is a description of five Christmas monsters on youtube.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wBTWD4-GCJI&amp;t=254s\" target=\"_blank\">Discover 5 Legendary Christmas Creatures [Christmas Mythology] - YouTube</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T17:48:29-08:00","id":1469216,"title":"","content":"I found a book that can give inspiration on how to incorporate Christmas traditions into the <i>Winter Court.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Winter Solstice: The Sacred Traditions of Christmas</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Many of us long for an alternative to the commercial industry Christmas has become. This beautifully illustrated, full-color book, brimming with folklore, stories, recipes, games, activities, decorating ideas, songs, and other resources, will help families who are &quot;burned out&quot; on Christmas create alternative celebrations more in keeping with the heartful spirit of the original Winter Solstice festivals.<br /> <br /> Each chapter provides cross-cultural connections to the ideas, customs, and icons of Christmas. Even when Matthews seems to be reaching a bit, it makes for engaging reading, and provides the rest of us with a way to connect with America's (and much of the Western World's) most important holiday season. It's especially engaging to know the origins of certain figures and beliefs; rarely are the origins religious, but cultural and traditional. [My favorite chapter was on the Twelve Days of Christmas.] The presentation of faith-free rituals at the end of each chapter was especially welcome, and I have already incorporated some small, new traditions into my holiday activities. How do the Winter Solstice, Yule, gifts, evergreens, lights, mummers plays, frivolity, and abundance of feasting come into the picture? This book researches Christmas's earliest pagan customs and traditions. I did enjoy the perspective on the twelve days of Christmas, which emphasizes the festival aspect of this season spanning many days; our commercial society has lost the festival aspect in favor of celebrating a single holiday. At the center of the season, whether you are a pagan, Christian, or otherwise, is the Winter Solstice, the death and rebirth of the sun, and I plan to try some activities suggested in this book to mark that event. We are drawn to the hearth, we admire twinkling lights, and we keep candlelight vigils in celebration of the coming of the sun of light into the world.<br /> <br /> You can order the book here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Winter-Solstice-Sacred-Traditions-Christmas/dp/0835608344/ref=cm_cr_arp_d_product_top?ie=UTF8\" target=\"_blank\">The Winter Solstice: The Sacred Traditions of Christmas: Matthews, John, Matthews, Caitlin: 9780835608343: Amazon.com: Books</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T16:42:25-08:00","id":1469281,"title":"","content":"<i><b>The Old Magic of Christmas: Yuletide Traditions for the Darkest Days of the Year<br /> 'Tis the Season for Witches, Elves, and a Legion of Ghosts</b></i><br /> <br /> Not so very long ago, Yuletide was as much a chilling season of ghosts and witches as it was a festival of goodwill. In The Old Magic of Christmas, you'll rub elbows with veiled spirits, learn the true perils of elves, and discover a bestiary of enchanted creatures. Rife with the more frightful characters from folklore and the season's most petulant ghosts, this book takes you on a spooky sleigh ride from the silvered firs of a winter forest to the mirrored halls of the Snow Queen. Along the way, you'll discover how to bring the festivities into your home with cookie recipes and craft instructions, as well as tips for delving more deeply into your relationship with the unseen.<br /> <br /> I finally understood that part of the song, &quot;The Most Wonderful Time of the Year&quot; when it spoke of scary ghost stories and tales of Christmases long time ago, since the only ghost story I ever heard connected with Christmas was &quot;A Christmas Carol&quot;. Here is a collection of old myths and legends that are truly delightfully creepy, and understandable, since the Longest Night of the Year seemed to make Winter stretch interminably. Most of these tales were designed to scare children into behaving and being careful as some of the more gruesome characters were actually considered out to get them otherwise. The Norse myths also make a respectable showing here as these winter myths, many of them came from that region. Here, we have the Wild Hunt and mysterious Odin as an origin for Santa Claus and the goddess Perchta. We also find Befana, the old woman wanderer who belatedly followed the Three Kings and is forever granting small gifts to children on her journeys in the hope of one day finding the Christ Child. This is a book that takes one into the darkest part of the year, where more than Winter can send a chill down the spine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/product-reviews/0738733342/ref=acr_dp_hist_5?ie=UTF8&amp;filterByStar=five_star&amp;reviewerType=all_reviews#reviews-filter-bar\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon.com: Customer reviews: The Old Magic of Christmas: Yuletide Traditions for the Darkest Days of the Year</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T13:28:44-08:00","id":1470068,"title":"","content":"I was looking for free christmas movies on <b><i>Youtube</i></b> and was surprised to find <i>Coraline</i>. This movie has a strong <i>Changeling: The Lost </i>tone, with the other mother and other father being very similiar to fetches.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=024HhcLQ_eM&amp;t=5233s\" target=\"_blank\">Coraline full movie - YouTube</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T13:30:48-08:00","id":1470069,"title":"","content":"Youtube also has <b><i>The Snow Queen</i></b> in Cartoon form.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-AQc0BGWskM\" target=\"_blank\">Snow Queen - YouTube</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T11:31:45-08:00","id":1470795,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">With Christmas just around the corner, I would like to recommend the 2015 horror movie <b><i>Krampus.</i></b> It has a strong <b><i>Changeling: The Lost </i></b>tone, with the characters being spirited away to a type of winter Christmas hell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Krampus\u201d is a film that has many factors to enjoy. Between the actually scary monsters, the comedy, and the amazing character development, this movie will become a future cult classic. \u201cKrampus\u201d centers around a dysfunctional family who don\u2019t get along. And after they finally push little Max to the limit, he loses the last of the family\u2019s Christmas spirit, and summons Krampus. Krampus and his helpers kidnap put Max and his family through crisis, and as the situation becomes more dangerous, the family starts to finally get along. The thing that\u2019s so great about \u201cKrampus\u201d is that it covers a topic that I don\u2019t think we see enough: how people should stop judging others for thinking differently. It\u2019s a topic that seems to grow more important as time goes on since 2020, and it displays it perfectly. Despite having great horror sequences, my favorite parts of the film is the character development as the family members learning to tolerate and help each other during a crisis. It puts great emphasis on just how ridiculous it is to not get along with someone because they\u2019re different from you, and how you should put that aside and focus on who they are as a person. It accidentally displays how many people feel right now in the world, just wanting things to be the way they used to be, and for people to get along again. I love seeing the difference in the characters from the beginning and end of the film. The horror sequences are very entertaining, and actually pretty damn scary. And although it\u2019s not 100% culturally accurate to the legend of Krampus, it works. The special effects look great, and the cast does pretty good performances. The comedy doesn\u2019t always hit the spot for me, but most of the time, it does. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T08:49:16-08:00","id":1470859,"title":"","content":"Here is another detailed description of <b><i>Krampus</i></b>. I think if you draw on Brom's <b><i>Krampus</i></b><b><i> the Yule King</i></b>, <i><b>Krampus Night</b></i>, and the 2015 <i><b>Krampus</b></i> movie you would have a lot of good material for a Changeling Christmas chronicle that portrayed Krampus as a True Fae.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tuSrajd9D8k\" target=\"_blank\">Krampus: Origins of the Yuletide Monster | Monstrum - YouTube</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T17:45:45-08:00","id":1470896,"title":"","content":"I found that you can watch <b><i>The Nightmare Before Christmas</i></b> on youtube.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Edit by Mod: No pirated movies on here.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1